[1mTwo constraints worth knowing.[22m The default CMake build sets no [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m, so the C library's [38;5;10massert()[0m calls are live and a malformed stream aborts the process instead of returning — inflate inputs are therefore kept well-formed, plus the error paths that provably do not trip an assertion. Separately, [38;5;10mcp_stored[0m copies [38;5;10mLEN[0m bytes with no output-bounds check at all, so combining a stored block with an undersized output buffer corrupts the heap inside the C library; the truncation fuzzer excludes stored blocks for that reason. Both limits are documented in the test files.[0m[0m
